# First-run setup wizard

When changing operator-facing UI or behavior, check whether the first-run wizard
(`src/renderer/src/features/setup-wizard/`) and Settings **Open setup assistant** still
match. If the change belongs in first-run, update the wizard (and its tests/docs)
in the **same PR**.

Trigger surfaces:

- SteamCMD path / install / status copy
- Default base folder
- Desktop shell (tray, Start with Windows, density)
- Show server console on start
- Create server / Import cluster join (`listKnownClusterOptions`, `ServerForm`,
  `ImportInstallWizard`)
- Cluster ID/dir validation (`createClusterModel`, `CreateClusterIdentityStep`)
- Overview empty CTAs
- Shared atoms used in the wizard (`PathField`, `ReadonlyPath`, `AppSurfaceCard`,
  `EmptyState`)

Do not add first-run-only chrome that Settings does not already own. Telemetry
consent is #309 — do not add it here.

## Operator copy and wizard chrome

Write helper text for the operator (what they see, why it helps), not an
inventory of steps. YARK is a **server manager** for ASA dedicated servers on
this PC — not a game client and not “localhost”. Canonical sentences, the
SteamCMD vs profile vs Install files distinction, and examples:
[docs/design-system.md](../../docs/design-system.md#operator-facing-copy).

`SetupWizard` uses `closeOnClickOutside={false}` so Skip / Close / Back is
explicit. Keep **Back** on the last first-run step (**First server**).
